Hi people,

This issue has been sorted. In the end I used a detection function created in the R package Distance and ditched the dummy ddf. This is because of the problem of estimating dsm uncertainty with a dummy ddf. The dummy ddf I was using did not have detection function uncertainty associated with it that "dsm.var.gam" was looking for. Note that when using the argument "ddf.obj=NULL", the "dsm.var.gam" function won't try to estimate detection function uncertainty.

For the sake of someone else having the same issue as me, I once received this error when I tried to predict a dsm model:

"Error in if (score > best$score && (!only.loose || (lmin <= dmin && lmax >=  : missing value where TRUE/FALSE needed"

This error was caused when the predicted abundance for each grid cell was too high (awful model!) and R replaced the predicted value with "Inf". "Inf" is short for Infinity!

Thank you kindly to David Miller for helping me out of this bother!

Greg Lollback

