Natalie, I would try method 3.  We have discussed this in the past with respect to polar bear surveys.  If you adopt this strategy, decide on some maximum distance beyond which you would not use the distance.  This might for example be half-way to the next transect.  Also use mcds (multiple-covariate distance sampling) for the analysis, with group size and whether detection as direct or via tracks as covariates.

